meta {
  name: Check password breaches
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/password/breaches?prefix=5BAA6
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  prefix: 5BAA6
}

docs {
  # Check password breaches

  Returns every known breached password hash suffix sharing a given five
  character SHA-1 prefix, from the Have I Been Pwned Pwned Passwords data set.
  Backs the password checker mashup and is available to the mobile and desktop
  clients.

  ## Privacy model (k-anonymity)

  This endpoint never receives a password, and never receives a complete hash.
  The caller computes the SHA-1 of the candidate password locally, uppercases
  it, sends only the **first five characters**, and compares the remaining 35
  character suffix against the returned map itself. A match means the password
  appears in a known breach.

  `5BAA6` is the prefix of the SHA-1 of the password `password`, which is why it
  makes a good smoke test: the suffix `1E4C9B93F3F0682250B6CF8331B7EE68FD8`
  will be present with a very large count.

  Padding decoys returned by the upstream service (count 0) are removed before
  the response is sent, so every entry in `suffixes` is a real breach count.

  ## Auth

  None. The upstream service requires no API key.

  ## Parameters

  - `prefix` (string, required) — exactly five hexadecimal characters. Lower
    case is accepted and upper-cased by the service. Anything else is a 400.

  ## Responses

  ### 200 OK — lookup performed

  {
    "prefix": "5BAA6",
    "count": 963,
    "suffixes": {
      "1E4C9B93F3F0682250B6CF8331B7EE68FD8": 10437277
    }
  }

  Fields:

  - `prefix` (string) — the prefix that was looked up, upper-cased.
  - `count` (number) — how many real suffixes were returned.
  - `suffixes` (object) — 35 character hash suffix to number of breaches.

  A prefix matching nothing returns `count: 0` and an empty `suffixes` object,
  not a 404: "no known breach" is a successful answer.

  ### 400 Bad Request — malformed prefix

  {
    "statusCode": 400,
    "error": "Bad Request",
    "message": "Parameter \"prefix\" must be exactly five hexadecimal characters.",
    "validation": [],
    "url": "/api/v1/password/breaches?prefix=NOTHEX",
    "method": "GET"
  }

  ### 502 Bad Gateway — upstream unavailable

  Have I Been Pwned is unreachable, timed out after 3 seconds, or answered a
  non-2xx status.

  {
    "statusCode": 502,
    "error": "Bad Gateway",
    "message": "The breach lookup service is unavailable.",
    "validation": [],
    "url": "/api/v1/password/breaches?prefix=5BAA6",
    "method": "GET"
  }
}
